From 3d59e6ae97a95a6c267894a47dd6b15f438f4e19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:13:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: soundwire: qcom: recover the bus when auto enumeration
 fails

Bit 11 of the interrupt status, AUTO_ENUM_FAILED, fell through to the
"unknown interrupt" default. On the ASUS Zenbook A16 it was raised on
an s2idle resume, after which both WSA8845 on that bus stayed
UNATTACHED until a later bus clash happened to run the deferred
recovery (about a minute and two suspend cycles later).

Schedule the same recovery as for a bus clash.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 5551c0bf28ea..ee5d39f3959a 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -974,6 +974,19 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_swrm_irq_handler(int irq, void *dev_id)
 			case SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_SPECIAL_CMD_ID_FINISHED:
 				complete(&ctrl->broadcast);
 				break;
+			case SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_AUTO_ENUM_FAILED:
+				/*
+				 * Peripherals that failed hardware enumeration
+				 * stay unattached until something resets the
+				 * bus; let the clash recovery do that.
+				 */
+				dev_err_ratelimited(ctrl->dev,
+					"%s: SWR auto enumeration failed\n",
+					__func__);
+				atomic_inc(&ctrl->recovery_pending);
+				if (READ_ONCE(ctrl->recovery_ready))
+					schedule_work(&ctrl->recovery_work);
+				break;
 			case SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_BUS_RESET_FINISHED_V2:
 				break;
 			case SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_CLK_STOP_FINISHED_V2:
